// # 2026-11-06 Fleet Drift Audit — ooda vs master/main (First Report)
//
// Logline: First output of buildbox/drift — a read-only audit of the
//          nine umbrella checkouts comparing live github tips of the
//          ooda integration branch against legacy master/main refs,
//          with ancestry verdicts from remote-tracking objects.
//
// Setup:   Binary /tmp/drift_main built from buildbox/drift/drift_main.oo
//          via oodac.real. Runtime env: OODA_NO_JAIL=1,
//          OO_LIST_AMBIENT_QUOTA=8589934592 (unjailed children so ssh
//          can reach ~/.ssh for ls-remote). No fetch, no mutation:
//          ancestry uses refs/remotes/github/* objects only; a stale
//          tracking ref would be flagged, never refreshed. None found.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Method.
//   2. Per-repo table.
//   3. The one DIVERGED case analyzed.
//   4. Reconcile proposals (manager executes all pushes).

== 1. Method ==

Per repo: `git ls-remote github refs/heads/ooda refs/heads/master
refs/heads/main` for live tips, then `git rev-list --left-right
--count refs/remotes/github/ooda...refs/remotes/github/<legacy>` for
ancestry. Verdicts: SYNC (0,0) / FF-ABLE (ooda ahead only) /
BEHIND (legacy ahead only) / DIVERGED (both) / UNFETCHED / ERR.

